WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.826 --> 00:00:20.696
Daisy's heart pounded. "Please don't send Sunny away, Jon!

2
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.420
He ran off, but he felt me slipping—and stopped right away!"

3
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.160
"That's good to hear," Jan said.

4
00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:34.196
"Yes, but . . ." Jon shook his head.

5
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.580
"We have enough to do without a green horse to train."

6
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.700
Daisy dismounted. "Sunny also found his way back to the farm.

7
00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.520
He knows it's his home!"

8
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.860
"He's a great horse," Jan said sadly. "But Jon's right.

9
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:10.890
If an experienced young rider can't control him on the trail, he's too green.

10
00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.890
We can't keep him."

11
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:18.630
"I have to tell you something." Daisy took a deep breath.

12
00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:23.950
"I'm not an experienced rider. I lied because I wanted to ride Sunny."

13
00:01:24.822 --> 00:01:27.709
"What?" Jan looked shocked.

14
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:32.270
"During the lesson I was so focused on Grace, I didn't even notice!"

15
00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.830
"I'm sorry." Daisy felt miserable.

16
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:41.290
"But please don't send Sunny back. It's my fault he ran away."

17
00:01:41.855 --> 00:01:45.279
Jon and Jan stared at each other.

18
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:50.109
Daisy was near tears. "I wanted to help Sunny," she thought.

19
00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.410
"Instead I made things worse—way worse!"

20
00:01:54.243 --> 00:02:01.821
Squeal! Just then a pig charged into the barn.

21
00:02:01.822 --> 00:02:07.404
"Hubert! He escaped again!" Kaleem yelled.

22
00:02:07.405 --> 00:02:09.835
Blossom whinnied and backed up.

23
00:02:09.836 --> 00:02:15.859
Ozzy spun in a circle, looking terrified. Grace looked terrified too.

24
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.800
But Sunny immediately pricked his ears.

25
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.239
"It's the pig!" he said happily.

26
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.580
Daisy suddenly got an idea.

27
00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:30.320
"The other horses are terrified, Sunny," she whispered.

28
00:02:30.947 --> 00:02:34.140
"We have to get Hubert out of here."

29
00:02:34.141 --> 00:02:35.904
"No problem!"

30
00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.340
Daisy led the horse toward Hubert.

31
00:02:42.905 --> 00:02:50.987
"Get back, pig!" Sunny said.

32
00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:55.570
Hubert squealed loudly as Daisy kept her hand on Sunny's reins.

33
00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.070
Then together they backed Hubert out the doors!

34
00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:10.443
"I've got him now!" Kaleem said, chasing Hubert back into the pigpen.

35
00:03:10.444 --> 00:03:14.326
Ozzy and Blossom quickly settled down.

36
00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.829
"Good thinking, Daisy!" Jan said.

37
00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:22.290
"And great horse handling—Sunny stayed so calm."

38
00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.970
Daisy grinned. "I told you, he's a great horse!"

39
00:03:29.822 --> 00:03:37.135
Jon nodded. "But he's still green, and we're so busy. I don't think—"

40
00:03:37.136 --> 00:03:41.947
"What if we helped out?" Daisy looked at Kaleem and Grace, who nodded.

41
00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:45.070
"School will be out soon, so we can come often."

42
00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.250
"I can help with other stuff around the farm too," Kaleem said.

43
00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.550
Jan and Jon stared at each other again.

44
00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:58.430
Daisy held her breath. "Please say yes," she thought. "Please."

45
00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.870
"What do you think?" Jan asked softly.

46
00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:09.250
"I think . . ." Jon said. "A green horse who stays calm under pressure is worth training."

47
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.030
The kids cheered.

48
00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:17.710
As soon as everyone moved away, Daisy hugged Sunny.

49
00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.970
"I'm sorry I almost ruined things for you."

50
00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:25.590
"No problem," Sunny said. "We had a great trail ride together!"

51
00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:29.349
Daisy nodded. "Yes, but if I hadn't—"

52
00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.030
"Daisy?"

53
00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.470
Daisy spun around.

54
00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.430
Grace stood there with a confused expression.

55
00:04:36.028 --> 00:04:36.569
"Were you just. . . ?"

56
00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:42.330
"Yes! I can talk to animals!" Daisy blurted out.

57
00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.470
"It sounds crazy, and I can tell you more, but—"

58
00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:49.290
"I knew it!" Grace said, smiling.

59
00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:53.310
"That's why you're so good with animals, isn't it?"

60
00:04:54.197 --> 00:04:56.149
Bzzz. Bzzz.

61
00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.230
"Oh no!" Daisy thought.

62
00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.790
Beatrice was hovering behind her!

63
00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:04.630
Had the bee just heard Daisy tell Grace her secret?
